          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong star-polycategory
            is to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-autonomous+category"} star-autonomous category
            what a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategory"} multicategory
            is to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polycategory"} polycategory
            in which every object has a dual. As such it is a model of classical linear logic with no connectives except negation.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p There are a number of candidate definitions, depending on what we make strict.
          %h3#definition_in_terms_of_duals Definition in terms of duals
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an object in a symmetric polycategory. A
            %em dual
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            comprises an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*
            together with a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo ;
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(A,A^*;-)
            making the induced composition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ;
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo ;
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\Gamma;A,\Delta)\to Hom(\Gamma,A^*;\Delta)
            a bijection for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
          %p
            A symmetric
            %em star-polycategory
            is a symmetric polycategory in which every object has a dual.
          %h3#strict_involution Strict involution
          %p
            In any star-polycategory there is an isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo *
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{**}\cong A
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{**}=A
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Hyland"} Hyland, Sec 5.3
          %ul
            %li
              A collection of objects, together with an involution operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^*
              (so
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{**}=A
            %li
              For lists
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              of objects, a set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ;
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\Gamma;\Delta)
            %li
              %em Exchange and negation structure:
              Two lists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              induce a single list
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma^*,\Delta
              by concatenating
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma^*
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Π
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma^*,\Delta\to\Pi^*,\Sigma
              should induce a function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ;
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Π
                      %mo ;
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\Gamma;\Delta)\to \Hom(\Pi;\Sigma)
            %li
              For each object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ;
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(A;A)
            %li
              For lists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Π
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma,\Delta,\Pi,\Sigma
              and objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ;
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Π
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo ;
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Π
                      %mo ;
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\Gamma;A,\Delta)\times Hom(\Pi,A;\Sigma)\to Hom(\Gamma,\Pi;\Delta,\Sigma)
              %p respecting the exchange and negation structure, and satisfying the same identity and associativity laws as for an ordinary polycategory.
          %p
            In the last axiom, “respecting the exchange and negation structure” has two pieces. The first, more obvious, one is that the composition functions are natural with respect to object-preserving bijections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 1
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 2
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_1^*,\Delta_1 \to \Gamma_2^*,\Delta_2
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 2
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1^*,\Sigma_1 \to \Pi_2^*,\Sigma_2
            which leave the
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the same as composing along
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ;
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Π
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo ;
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo ∘
                                %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Π
                          %mo ;
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo *
                          %mo ;
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Π
                          %mo ;
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo *
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Π
                          %mo ;
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo *
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo *
                          %mo ;
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo ∘
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi A
                                    %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Π
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ;
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Hom(\Gamma;A,\Delta) \times Hom(\Pi,A;\Sigma) &amp;\xrightarrow{\circ_A} &amp; Hom(\Gamma,\Pi;\Delta,\Sigma) \\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow \\
                  Hom(\Gamma,A^*;\Delta) \times Hom(\Pi;A^*,\Sigma) &amp;&amp; \downarrow \\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow \\
                  Hom(\Pi;A^*,\Sigma) \times Hom(\Gamma,A^*;\Delta) &amp; \xrightarrow{\circ_{A^*}} &amp; Hom(\Pi,\Gamma;\Sigma,\Delta)
                  }
          %p
            Note that because of symmetry, we can get away with requiring composition only when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the first object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,\Delta
            and the last object in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi,A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with arbitrary placement in these lists, then there would be an axiom asserting that these compositions are invariant with respect to permutations that rearrange the location of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,\Delta
            and last in
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi,A
          %h3#entries_only Entries only
          %p
            In a star-polycategory we have natural bijections
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ;
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ;
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ;
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\Gamma;\Delta)\cong Hom(-;\Gamma^*,\Delta)\cong Hom(\Gamma,\Delta^*;-)
          %ul
            %li
              A collection of objects, together with an involution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^*
              (so
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{**}=A
            %li
              For any list
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              of objects, a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\Gamma)
              of “morphisms”.
            %li
              Each object-preserving-bijection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma\to \Delta
              should induce a function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\Gamma)\to \Hom(\Delta)
            %li
              For each object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(A,A^*)
            %li
              For lists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma,\Delta
              and objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\Gamma,A)\times Hom(A^*,\Delta)\to Hom(\Gamma,\Delta)
              %p respecting the exchange structure and satisfying identity and associativity laws.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Recall that a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linearly+distributive+category"} linearly distributive category
                can be understood as a representable polycategory. It is star-autonomous if the corresponding polycategory is a star-polycategory.
            %li
              %p
                For example,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
                form a (weak) star-polycategory. The objects are categories,
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mo *
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*=A^{\mathrm{op}}
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi Cat
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                        %mi …
                        %mo ×
                        %mi …
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(A_1,\dots,A_n)=Cat(A_1\dots\times\dots A_n,\mathbf{Set})
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coends"} coends
            %li
              %p
                The unit interval forms a thin star polycategory. The objects are real numbers in the interval
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mo *
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*=(1-A)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(A_1,\dots A_n)
                is inhabited if
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                          %mi n
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i=1}^n A_i = 1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                with anything except
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %li
              %p
                More generally, any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effect+algebra"} effect algebra
                forms a thin star-polycategory in the same way. Sequences
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                for which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\Gamma)
                is inhabited are usually called “tests”. The tensor in the polycategorical sense is the partial monoid in the effect algebra sense.
          %h2#references References
